Z||000024||ChopTop||05-12-2001||11:18 AM||||Actually my car can be a little scary to drive.  I believe the stock height of the Fiero is 46 inches.  I have the Suspension Techniques springs on, which drops it approximately two inches, than the three inch choptop, which makes my car around 41 high.  I was run off the road once, and have cars/SUVs pull in my lane frequently.  Drivers simply don't see the car.  But I've also rattled a few people too by pulling up beside them, again because they had no idea a car was there.  And I try never to pull up too closely behind anyone, in the event they decide to back up.  I generally try to stay to the very right of the lane.  I figure they may not be able to see me in their rear view mirror, but should be able to see me in their side mirror.  It can be quite entertaining to watch people whipping their necks around looking for the blaring horn.  The funny thing is I still want it lower, and hope to install dropped spindles and coil overs someday.  ||||reg||1
Z||000025||rogergarrison||05-13-2001||04:59 AM||||not fiero related, but I know about unexpected back ups. A gf gave me her 86 Vette to fix the front bumper she messed up and get a new set of tires put on. I was behind a Dodge minivan waiting to go out on street. They pulled out halfway and stopped, then backed up and ran rite into it. Anyway I raised a little hell since it wasnt even my car. There insurance co paid to repaint the front bumper for me, for lots more than I was going to do it for. Dawn was tickled to death when I told her the new tires were free and gave her a couple hundred dollars back too. (ps screw the insur co, theyve done it to me a million times)||||reg||1
Z||000026||Cozmo||05-13-2001||07:25 AM||||You learn new ways of getting in and out of cars when you own a Fiero...<BR>If I drive my Targa for a few days with the top off then switch to my "hardtop" Fiero,<BR>I bang the s**t out of my head on the roof a few times until I remember to "duck and roll" again... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><B>C02M0</B> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000027||Spektyr||05-13-2001||02:57 PM||||I couldn't drive a chop top.  I'm almost too tall to drive it stock.<P>Where I park at work I usually end up next to a curb on my driver's side, and that's about level with the floorboards.  Definitely makes getting out harder.<P>Lean left, grab top of door frame with right hand, back of door frame with left hand.  Put left foot on curb, right foot at joint where gas tank hump and floorboard meet.  Push off with right foot and pull with both arms.  Stand up.<P>Took me a few tries to get it right the first time, was afraid I was going to have to crawl out.  My legs are long enough that I usually tilt the wheel all the way up so I can get my right knee underneath the steering wheel.<P>Hey, but the best things in life are usually the ones that aren't easy to do.||||reg||1
Z||000028||fldevel||05-14-2001||02:48 PM|||| u would think the designers knowing how low the fieros where would actualy put the "OH **** " handles in the fieros to help us get out ...||||reg||1
Z||000029||Ken Wittlief||05-14-2001||03:48 PM||||I really liked it when I had a full sized dodge van and I could see over the tops of SUVs, and I blocked THEIR view when I pulled up along side them at a driveway exit! But I did have to reach down pretty far at the ATM drive up.<P> With my fiero now I can see UNDER SUVs  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> and I have to reach way up to the ATM driveup.<P>I have had a few people start to pull out in from side streets on me already (car has been on the road less than a month) I think I will put some fog lights or something under the front bumper and wire then as running lights.<P>  the fiero is a very humble car. (Humble: close to the earth).||||reg||1
Z||000030||JSocha||05-14-2001||05:14 PM||||I finally learned how to get into mine.<P>Sit down in the drivers seat first and then twist my fat butt and swing my legs in to the foot wells.<P>A Fiero being low has one distinct advantage over most cars.  When being chased by police, you can duck behind a low bush, hide while the police mozy righ on by.  Then you can pull out go the other way or follow behind them.<P>Confuse the heck out of them...make them think that they were going so fast they passed righ on by you  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
